                        "recommendationid": "237931441",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199003002346",
                            "num_reviews": 13,
                            "playtime_forever": 731,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 233,
                            "playtime_at_review": 731,
                            "last_played": 1792243346
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you can get it for cheap it will probably entertain you for some time. I think this game is fine as a game, but doesn't make for a good roguelike. I believe it would have been better if you could unlock weapons as you played and choose them before starting a run. The reason is that the pool of items is much smaller than most roguelikes/lites, so a lot of the time you play with the same few weapons. If there's one in particular, you just have to hope you get it with good affixes, because enemies starting from the third area get super tanky. \r\n\r\nWhile you could for example beat dead cells bc0 on a fresh file without much issue, it's extremely unlikely in the game because the stat buffs and gadgets you unlock influence your stats a lot more than the random buffs you get. \r\n\r\nI would say that overall I had a good enough time (especially given that I paid €1,20), but I wish just wish it was better in the areas I described.",
